The ViSQOL-compatible metric implements the audio (music) mode only; it is not intended for
speech quality estimation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled data: ViSQOL audio-mode SVR model
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File:     data/visqol/libsvm_nu_svr_model.txt (included unchanged)
Source:   https://github.com/google/visqol  (model/libsvm_nu_svr_model.txt,
          branch master, retrieved 2026-11-12)
SHA-256:  1e8246ed33bf36dc5c859351f7110f2cd31f98661989715c0fcf974ec48d3e2e
Owner:    Google LLC
License:  Apache License, Version 2.0 — full text in data/visqol/LICENSE-Apache-2.0
          (also https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)

The file is a libsvm nu-SVR model (RBF kernel, 32 features, 317 support vectors) that maps
per-band similarity to MOS in ViSQOL's audio mode. It is used here as data only; the code
that reads and evaluates it was written from the libsvm format documentation.
